10988:   { name: 'runtime:prompt_envelope_review_gate', level: 'L4', category: 'runtime-behavior', owner: 'core/review-run', rationale: 'Enabled full-envelope reviewer roles require one integrity-verified content-addressed review-run Prompt Envelope whose story, role/lane, round, ReviewRun, HEAD, materialHash and storyFilesHash equal the signed ReviewRun. The envelope also binds the exact standard story-dispatch prompt bytes and the selected host render identity: Claude Code/CLI map explicitly to Claude and Codex/CLI map explicitly to Codex. A nonblank explicit unsupported provider is preserved as unknown and takes precedence over competing Codex/Claude environment inference; antigravity/agy, fake, unknown, or absent providers fail closed because they have no PromptHost render identity. Runtime-owned/global-thin, registry, and explicit full-asset hosts all bind the same canonical role-specific body-free bootstrap separately from the selected role-body render, so total input is honestly bootstrap plus exactly one selected body rather than a false byte-exact mirror claim. review_run_start refuses missing dispatch provenance, and later selected-host bootstrap drift invalidates the run. review_run_start delivers and records the exact assembledPrompt bytes, promptHash must equal the envelope digest, canonical runtime/role/task assembly is recomputed, ReviewPass signs the same envelopeId, and REVIEW/quorum consumers use the shared verifier. The assurance floor consumes signed host-verdict rounds; quorum_submit is the mechanical boundary that refuses to emit those rounds unless all eligible envelope-bound reviewer passes are current.', gateConsumer: 'storyMachine.canPassReview REVIEW to TEST gate and quorum_submit reviewer-pass admission boundary; review assurance floor consumes resulting host-verdict rounds' },
